{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Structured Agent Fallback Output.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Structured Agent Fallback Output.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"structured agent fallback output structured agent fallback output","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Structured Agent Fallback Output.md","fileName":"Structured Agent Fallback Output.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Structured Agent Fallback Output","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Structured Agent Fallback Output.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Structured Agent Fallback Output.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"structured agent fallback output structured agent fallback output","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Structured Agent Fallback Output.md","fileName":"Structured Agent Fallback Output.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Structured Agent Fallback Output","heading":"Structured Agent Fallback Output","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A structured agent fallback preserves the output contract when model output is invalid. If JSON parsing, required-field checks, enumeration checks, or range checks fail, application code emits a known safe result with an unknown or medium-risk classification, zero confidence, and a recommendation for manual inspection.\n\nThe fallback prevents downstream parsers from failing unpredictably or treating missing data as success. It does not disguise the model error: the output explicitly records that validation failed and directs the workflow toward a conservative path.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaif